`karr --help` is hand-formatted; `karr <cmd> --help` is MooX::Options' long format:

    --claimed_by: String
        Filter by claim owner
    ...
                                                                            (two lines of spaces)
    --usage:
        show a short help message
    -h: ...  --help: ...  --man: ...

Three problems for a reader, and for an agent that pipes through head/tail (k263):

1. Option names print with underscores (`--claimed_by`, `--not_blocked`, `--add_tag`, `--append_body`, `--depends_on`, `--claude_skill`, `--new_board`, `--accept_foreign_board`, `--write_to`, `--hide_no_board`) while the USAGE line right above them, README.md and the skill spell them with hyphens. Both spellings parse, but the help contradicts the docs one screen apart.
2. Two lines of trailing whitespace before the --usage block.
3. `--usage`, `-h`, `--help`, `--man` take four entries on every command, and `--dir`/`--quiet` repeat on all of them.

`karr <cmd> -h` (the compact format) is already much better: one line per option, `--claim=String`.

## What to build

Make `--help` render the compact form, or a house renderer over the option metadata that prints hyphenated names one per line with the root options in a trailing OPTIONS block like the top-level help. MooX::Options' `usage_string`, per-option `format`, and its help hooks are the knobs; check whether an existing flag already emits hyphens before writing a renderer. The USAGE line stays. Listing the board's values for `--priority`/`--status`/`--class` when a board is found is nice, not required. Changes entry; the tests that snapshot help output need updating.

Also karr-foundation --help: the same MooX::Options long format, with --dry_run spelled with an underscore while README and the transcripts write --dry-run. Cover it in the same sweep.

Pointers: every Cmd declares use MooX::Options (usage_string => ...); Role::ExitCodes buffers STDERR around new_with_options and prints the diagnostic after the usage block (k263), so a renderer change must keep that ordering. Tests that pin help output: t/131-help-column-alignment.t (root), t/81-error-messages.t, t/256-dashed-option-after-flag.t, t/263-error-shows-working-command.t.
